  "notes": "Traditional nursery tune per the Wikipedia LilyPond score (3/8, G major), note values doubled to 3/4 and transposed G->C: 1-5-5 | 5-4321 | 1-6-6 | 6 || 1-5-5 | 5-4321 | 4-3-2 | 1. The 8-bar strain is played twice (two verses) = 16 bars. No pickup. Old version was an invented arpeggio melody, not the song. The real tune needs A4 (69) and a group of four eighths per phrase, which beginner limits (RH 60-67, no eighths) cannot hold, so it is checked against elementary limits."
